2026-09-27T07:22:15.7654394Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7654979Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7655485Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7657071Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7658354Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7658484Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7658761Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7659162Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7659468Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7659560Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7659761Z ================
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7659874Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7660038Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7660374Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7660570Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7660675Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7660928Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7661093Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7661221Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7661608Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7661934Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7662852Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7663573Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7663688Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7664088Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7664662Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7665143Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7665560Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7666142Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7666269Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7666556Z ========
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7666722Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7668146Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7669330Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7669545Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7669976Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7670734Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7671290Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7671804Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7672216Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7672667Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7672893Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7673148Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7673284Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7674383Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7675414Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7675991Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7676788Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:22:15.7676989Z 
